A||||6||JasonS||Which is easier to fix???||||5||
Z||000000||JasonS||07-09-2001||09:25 AM||||Ok, here's my situation.  After I first bought my '84 (about a year ago now), I opened my door and heard a metal clanging.  Since then, I have to either leave my window down enough to reach inside and open the door, or leave my doors unlocked and reach in through the passenger's side to open the driver's door.  The other problem that adds to my misery is the passenger door lock doesn't unlock with the key, it sits there and spins.  Well, now it is rainy season in sunny Florida and I have to leave my window up, which means I have to look like an idiot leaning in from the passenger side to swing my door open and then walk to the other side.  Well, as you can probably guess, If I leave my windows up and forget that my passenger door is locked, I can't get into my car (I've done this twice). So my question is, what is eaiser to fix??? 1) My doorhandle on the drivers side, or 2) a lock that just spins when I put the key in on the passenger side?  Thanks in advance for any help,  Jason||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrgone||07-09-2001||11:59 AM||||actually im pretty sure its the same problem on both doors, and requires the same fix.<P>the clanging sound on the driver side door, is the rod that goes from the key lock to the interior lock switch. its just missing a little clip (a ziptie like thing) and hitting the door when you slam it.<P>the reason why the passenger door key just spins, is because the (possibly the same) rod is missing that clip.  i used a ziptie for a semi-temporary fix.<P>just take out all the door screws, armrest, and window crank. the window cran can be removed wither by a screwdriver or by sliding a rag in there and pulling on it.  pull off the door liner (dont worry about those white plastic things ripping through, they arent important.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_9.jpg">   <BR><B>86.5 2m4 5speed turd 241,000kms</B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierohoho||07-09-2001||02:12 PM||||JasonS, <BR>If your door handle on the drivers side is disconnected from the rod there is a small plastic clip the rod fell out of. <P>In my experience the clip is usually still either in the door handle or in the bottom of the door. <P>If you have a working hanlde on the passenger door take the interior panels off of both at the same time to compare. <P>You will see on the working handle how its set up. <P>Have the windows all the way up when you do this. <P>The lock rod has a different clip, this one is metal and should be on the back of the lock arm in the bottom of the door or on the rod maybe. <P>No special tools are needed to put these back on just a little time.<P>I'm not sure mrgone has the best way to remove the door handle as I have not tried it, but, I use a paper-clip with a small fish hook bend in the end to reach behind the door handle and grab the "c" clip and pull it loose. The fish hook bend only needs to be about as big as this "J" is to hook the clip.<P>Good luck and let us know how things work out or if you have any problems. <P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000003||JasonS||07-09-2001||02:23 PM||||Thanks guys, I'll give it a shot and let you know how it turns out.  It'll be nice to finally be able to open my door from the outside...||||reg||14
Z||000004||rogergarrison||07-09-2001||07:24 PM||||id fix the driver door obviously. would worry about the passenger door till your completely bored this winter.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierohoho||07-10-2001||04:01 AM||||I agree with Roger, if you have to use a part from the pass door to fix the drivers door go that route. The parts you might need are pretty standard so a junk yard should have any number of cars to get them out of so I still recomend pulling both door panels. Once you have access its an easy fix.<P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l||||reg||1
Z||000006||JasonS||07-10-2001||08:46 AM||||Thanks for the help.  It looks like I'll be headed to the junkyark to find the metal rod that connects the doorhandle to the lever.  I took the door panel off and the rod was no where to be found.  I don't want to break the passenger door handle to fix the driver's side.  If something is working in my car, I definately don't want to touch it for fear something else might break!<BR>thanks again,<BR>Jason||||reg||6
